    <!-- =====================================================================
         Category palette

         Seven families, one per kind of thing the app holds. Generated in
         OKLCH, not picked by eye: lightness is constant across the set
         (L 0.52 start, 0.38 end), so no family shouts louder than another and
         white text clears WCAG AA on every one (5.2:1 to 6.2:1). Chroma is 80%
         of what each hue can reach in sRGB, because holding chroma constant
         instead would drag the whole set down to the weakest hue's limit.

         The hue arc runs violet 310 -> green 150 and passes through the brand
         navy at 270. The brand gold (hue 78) is deliberately absent: it is the
         accent, and an accent that also means "one of seven categories" stops
         being an accent.

         A gradient's two stops share a hue and differ only in lightness. A
         gradient that also shifts hue is the thing that makes a UI look
         unconsidered.
         ===================================================================== -->
    <color name="category_identity_start">#8E34C1</color>
    <color name="category_identity_end">#5B1E7E</color>
    <color name="category_authority_start">#6046E2</color>
    <color name="category_authority_end">#3D249D</color>
    <color name="category_transport_start">#2868B9</color>
    <color name="category_transport_end">#164279</color>
    <color name="category_attestation_start">#2C728F</color>
    <color name="category_attestation_end">#19485C</color>
    <color name="category_exchange_start">#2D757B</color>
    <color name="category_exchange_end">#194B4F</color>
    <color name="category_integrity_start">#2D7867</color>
    <color name="category_integrity_end">#1A4C41</color>
    <color name="category_lifecycle_start">#2D7B44</color>
    <color name="category_lifecycle_end">#194F29</color>

